      "content": "I see the repository doesn't exist yet. Let me create a comprehensive starter structure for your ISP WiFi billing system. I'll set up the complete project architecture with all necessary files.\n\nSince you're starting from scratch, I'll create:\n1. **Project structure** - Monorepo with microservices\n2. **Backend services** - NestJS API with multi-tenant support\n3. **Frontend** - Next.js customer & admin portals\n4. **Database schemas** - PostgreSQL setup\n5. **Configuration files** - Docker, environment setup\n6. **Documentation** - Architecture guides\n\nLet me build this step by step. First, I need to know:\n\n**Quick Clarifications:**\n1. **GitHub Repo**: Do you have the repository created on GitHub yet? If not, I'll need you to create it first (it must exist before I can push code).\n2. **Tech Stack Confirmation**: Should I proceed with:\n   - **Backend**: Node.js + NestJS + GraphQL + REST\n   - **Frontend**: Next.js + React + TailwindCSS\n   - **Database**: PostgreSQL + Redis\n   - **Deployment**: Docker + Docker Compose (we can add K8s later)\n\n3. **Phase 1 Focus**: Should I start with:\n   - ✅ Authentication & Multi-tenant setup\n   - ✅ PPPoE Management core\n   - ✅ Hotspot Management core\n   - ✅ Billing Engine foundation\n   - ✅ Payment Gateway abstraction\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll generate:\n- Full folder structure\n- Base Docker setup\n- Database schemas\n- API boilerplate\n- UI component library\n- Complete documentation\n\n**Do you want me to proceed with creating the comprehensive starter code?** If yes, please create the GitHub repository first and share the link, or let me know the exact repo name and I can guide you through the setup!",
