      "content": "I need you to create the repository first. Here are the steps:\n\n1. Go to [github.com/new](https://github.com/new)\n2. Create a repository named `isp-wifi-billing-system`\n3. Initialize with a README\n4. Share the link or confirm it's created\n\nOnce created, I'll immediately push the entire project structure including:\n\n```\nisp-wifi-billing-system/\n├── apps/\n│   ├── admin-portal/          (Next.js - ISP admin dashboard)\n│   ├── customer-portal/       (Next.js - customer self-service)\n│   └── agent-app/             (Next.js - agent/reseller app)\n├── services/\n│   ├── auth-service/          (NestJS - JWT, MFA, OAuth2)\n│   ├── billing-service/       (NestJS - billing engine)\n│   ├── payment-service/       (NestJS - payment abstractions)\n│   ├── radius-service/        (NestJS - Radius/MikroTik)\n│   ├── notification-service/  (NestJS - SMS/Email/WhatsApp)\n│   ├── customer-service/      (NestJS - CRM)\n│   └── analytics-service/     (NestJS - reporting)\n├── packages/\n│   ├── ui-kit/                (Shared React components)\n│   ├── shared/                (Shared utilities & types)\n│   └── sdk/                   (Client SDK)\n├── docker-compose.yml\n├── docker-compose.prod.yml\n├── k8s/                       (Kubernetes manifests)\n├── db/\n│   ├── migrations/\n│   ├── seeds/\n│   └── schemas.sql\n├── .github/\n│   ├── workflows/             (CI/CD pipelines)\n├── docs/\n│   ├── architecture.md\n│   ├── api-docs.md\n│   ├── deployment.md\n│   └── database-schema.md\n└── README.md\n```\n\n**Create the repo and I'll immediately populate it with 50+ starter files!**",
