      "content": "I tried to create the repo branch but failed because the GitHub repository doesn't exist or I don't have access.\n\nWhat I did:\n- Attempted to create the branch \"main\" in nicholusmwirigikinoti-hub/isp-wifi-billing-system and got: \"Repository ... was not found or you don't have access to it.\"\n\nNext steps — pick one:\n\n1) You create the GitHub repo (recommended)\n   - Create a repository named isp-wifi-billing-system on your GitHub account (https://github.com/new). Initialize with a README (optional).\n   - Reply with the repo URL (or confirm it's created). I will then immediately push the full starter project into it (monorepo structure, services/apps, Docker, CI, docs, migrations, etc.).\n\n2) I generate the full starter project here as a downloadable archive\n   - I will create the complete folder structure and all starter files and provide them as a zip (I’ll paste file contents in chunks you can copy or provide a downloadable link).\n   - Use this if you prefer to create the repo and push from your machine.\n\n3) I give you a step-by-step CLI script to create the repo locally and push\n   - I’ll produce commands to initialize git, create the repo via GitHub CLI (gh), commit, and push — you run them and then I can push subsequent changes or create branches.\n\nPlease tell me which option you want and confirm the following defaults (I’ll use these unless you change them):\n- Backend: Node.js + NestJS (REST + GraphQL)\n- Frontend: Next.js + React + TailwindCSS\n- DB: PostgreSQL (Redis for sessions)\n- Container: Docker + Docker Compose (K8s later)\n\nIf you want me to proceed right away, say \"Proceed with option 1\" (and share the repo link when done) or \"Proceed with option 2\" to get the zip here.",
