      "content": "Direct answer: I’ll show a concrete, minimal rewrite plan and provide ready-to-drop-in code (DB migrations, NestJS controllers/services, and a Next.js admin page) so the “Main Admins” tab can edit every feature (PPPoE, Hotspot, Payments, OLT hosting, multi-country linking, white‑label/theme, agents/resellers, feature flags), plus an email verification flow for app access. Apply these files to your monorepo (or I can push them once you create the GitHub repo).\n\nWhat I changed / added (high-level)\n- Centralized settings per-tenant + platform-level settings so the Main Admin UI can toggle or edit every feature.\n- Feature flags and JSON settings enable/disable and configure modules: pppoe, hotspot, payments, olts, reseller, sms, notifications, themes.\n- Tenant -> multiple country mapping so one account can cover many countries with currencies & tax config.\n- OLT hosting model: OLT records with credentials and endpoints; API to provision/link ONUs to subscribers (vendor-specific adapters can be added).\n- Admin Settings API (NestJS) with GET/PUT endpoints and permission guard (main admin only).\n- Email verification flow (register -> send verification token -> verify) to allow app access by email verification.\n- Minimal Next.js admin page to edit settings from “Main Admins” tab.\n\nApply strategy\n1. Run DB migration SQL to add new tables/columns.\n2. Add NestJS modules: settings, olts, tenant-country, auth/email-verification.\n3. Add Admin UI page that calls the Settings API and renders toggles/forms for all features.\n4. Hook existing services (billing, radius, payment adapters) to read tenant_settings and feature flags at runtime to enable/disable behavior.\n5. Add email delivery provider (SMTP, SendGrid, Mailgun) for verification emails.\n\nKey files (drop these into your monorepo):\n- DB migration (create tables)\n- NestJS: settings controller + service + DTOs\n- NestJS: email verification service + controller\n- Next.js Admin page (Main Admins tab settings form)\nBelow are the files:\n\n```sql name=migrations/20260520_add_tenant_settings_and_olt.sql\n-- Tenant settings, multi-country mapping, OLT hosting, email verification token\n-- Run against your PostgreSQL DB (use your migration tool of choice)\n\n-- Tenants (if not already present)\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tenants (\n  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  name text NOT NULL,\n  slug text UNIQUE NOT NULL,\n  owner_user_id uuid,\n  created_at timestamptz DEFAULT now(),\n  updated_at timestamptz DEFAULT now()\n);\n\n-- Tenant countries (link tenant to multiple countries)\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tenant_countries (\n  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  tenant_id uuid REFERENCES tenants(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  country_code varchar(3) NOT NULL, -- ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 or alpha-2\n  currency_code varchar(3) NOT NULL,\n  tax_rate numeric DEFAULT 0, -- percent decimal (e.g., 18.00)\n  default boolean DEFAULT false,\n  created_at timestamptz DEFAULT now()\n);\nCREATE INDEX ON tenant_countries(tenant_id);\nCREATE UNIQUE INDEX tenant_country_unique ON tenant_countries(tenant_id, country_code);\n\n-- Tenant settings (JSON-based for flexible feature/config flags)\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tenant_settings (\n  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  tenant_id uuid REFERENCES tenants(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  settings jsonb NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}'::jsonb,\n  feature_flags jsonb NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}'::jsonb,\n  updated_by uuid,\n  created_at timestamptz DEFAULT now(),\n  updated_at timestamptz DEFAULT now()\n);\nCREATE INDEX ON tenant_settings(tenant_id);\n\n-- OLT hosting table (stores OLT endpoints/credentials)\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS olts (\n  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  tenant_id uuid REFERENCES tenants(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  vendor varchar(64) NOT NULL, -- e.g., huawei, zte, nokia\n  name text,\n  host text NOT NULL,\n  port integer,\n  api_type varchar(32) DEFAULT 'ssh', -- ssh, restconf, netconf, snmp\n  credentials jsonb, -- { \"user\": \"...\", \"pass\": \"...\" } (encrypt in application or vault)\n  region varchar(64),\n  management_url text,\n  enabled boolean DEFAULT true,\n  created_at timestamptz DEFAULT now(),\n  updated_at timestamptz DEFAULT now()\n);\nCREATE INDEX ON olts(tenant_id);\n\n-- Email verification tokens for new user registrations\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS email_verification_tokens (\n  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  user_id uuid REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  token varchar(128) UNIQUE NOT NULL,\n  expires_at timestamptz NOT NULL,\n  used boolean DEFAULT false,\n  created_at timestamptz DEFAULT now()\n);\nCREATE INDEX ON email_verification_tokens(user_id);\n```\n\n```typescript name=services/settings/settings.service.ts\nimport { Injectable, NotFoundException } from '@nestjs/common';\nimport { InjectRepository } from '@nestjs/typeorm';\nimport { Repository } from 'typeorm';\n\ninterface TenantSettings {\n  tenant_id: string;\n  settings: any;\n  feature_flags: any;\n  updated_by?: string;\n}\n\n@Injectable()\nexport class SettingsService {\n  constructor(\n    @InjectRepository('tenant_settings')\n    private readonly settingsRepo: Repository<any>,\n  ) {}\n\n  async getSettings(tenantId: string) {\n    const s = await this.settingsRepo.findOne({ where: { tenant_id: tenantId } });\n    if (!s) {\n      // return defaults\n      return {\n        tenant_id: tenantId,\n        settings: {\n          billing_cycle: 'monthly',\n          currency: 'USD',\n          theme: {},\n          pppoe: { enabled: true },\n          hotspot: { enabled: true },\n          payments: { enabled: true, providers: [] },\n          olts: { enabled: false }\n        },\n        feature_flags: {}\n      };\n    }\n    return s;\n  }\n\n  async upsertSettings(tenantId: string, payload: TenantSettings) {\n    const existing = await this.settingsRepo.findOne({ where: { tenant_id: tenantId } });\n    if (!existing) {\n      const newRow = this.settingsRepo.create({\n        tenant_id: tenantId,\n        settings: payload.settings || {},\n        feature_flags: payload.feature_flags || {},\n        updated_by: payload.updated_by\n      });\n      return this.settingsRepo.save(newRow);\n    }\n    existing.settings = payload.settings ?? existing.settings;\n    existing.feature_flags = payload.feature_flags ?? existing.feature_flags;\n    existing.updated_by = payload.updated_by;\n    existing.updated_at = new Date();\n    return this.settingsRepo.save(existing);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```typescript name=services/settings/settings.controller.ts\nimport { Controller, Get, Put, Param, Body, UseGuards, Req } from '@nestjs/common';\nimport { SettingsService } from './settings.service';\n// Assume you have AuthGuard + RolesGuard to allow only main admins\nimport { AuthGuard } from '../auth/auth.guard';\nimport { RolesGuard } from '../auth/roles.guard';\nimport { Roles } from '../auth/roles.decorator';\n\n@Controller('api/admin/:tenantId/settings')\n@UseGuards(AuthGuard, RolesGuard)\nexport class SettingsController {\n  constructor(private readonly settingsService: SettingsService) {}\n\n  @Get()\n  @Roles('SUPER_ADMIN', 'ISP_OWNER', 'FINANCE_MANAGER')\n  async get(@Param('tenantId') tenantId: string) {\n    return this.settingsService.getSettings(tenantId);\n  }\n\n  @Put()\n  @Roles('SUPER_ADMIN', 'ISP_OWNER')\n  async put(@Param('tenantId') tenantId: string, @Body() body: any, @Req() req: any) {\n    // body should contain { settings: {...}, feature_flags: {...} }\n    const updated = await this.settingsService.upsertSettings(tenantId, {\n      tenant_id: tenantId,\n      settings: body.settings,\n      feature_flags: body.feature_flags,\n      updated_by: req.user?.id\n    });\n    return updated;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```typescript name=services/olt/olt.service.ts\nimport { Injectable, Logger } from '@nestjs/common';\nimport { InjectRepository } from '@nestjs/typeorm';\nimport { Repository } from 'typeorm';\n\n/*\n  OLT Service provides CRUD for OLTs and a provision method (vendor adapters)\n  Vendor adapters should implement a common interface for provisioning/linking ONUs.\n*/\n\n@Injectable()\nexport class OltService {\n  private readonly logger = new Logger(OltService.name);\n\n  constructor(\n    @InjectRepository('olts')\n    private readonly oltRepo: Repository<any>,\n  ) {}\n\n  async createOlt(tenantId: string, payload: any) {\n    const record = this.oltRepo.create({ ...payload, tenant_id: tenantId });\n    return this.oltRepo.save(record);\n  }\n\n  async listForTenant(tenantId: string) {\n    return this.oltRepo.find({ where: { tenant_id: tenantId } });\n  }\n\n  async provisionOnu(oltId: string, onuParams: any) {\n    // Load OLT, call vendor adapter based on olt.vendor\n    const olt = await this.oltRepo.findOne({ where: { id: oltId } });\n    if (!olt) throw new Error('OLT not found');\n    // Example: if olt.vendor === 'huawei' => call HuaweiAdapter.provisionOnu(...)\n    // For now, just log and return a placeholder\n    this.logger.log(`Provisioning ONU on OLT ${oltId} vendor=${olt.vendor}`);\n    return { success: true, details: onuParams };\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```typescript name=services/auth/email-verification.service.ts\nimport { Injectable, Logger } from '@nestjs/common';\nimport { randomBytes } from 'crypto';\nimport { InjectRepository } from '@nestjs/typeorm';\nimport { Repository } from 'typeorm';\nimport * as dayjs from 'dayjs';\nimport { sendEmail } from '../../utils/mailer'; // implement mailer wrapper\n\n@Injectable()\nexport class EmailVerificationService {\n  private readonly logger = new Logger(EmailVerificationService.name);\n  constructor(\n    @InjectRepository('email_verification_tokens')\n    private readonly tokenRepo: Repository<any>,\n  ) {}\n\n  async createAndSend(user: any) {\n    const token = randomBytes(24).toString('hex');\n    const expiresAt = dayjs().add(24, 'hour').toDate();\n    const row = this.tokenRepo.create({\n      user_id: user.id,\n      token,\n      expires_at: expiresAt,\n    });\n    await this.tokenRepo.save(row);\n\n    const verificationUrl = `${process.env.APP_URL}/auth/verify-email?token=${token}`;\n    const subject = 'Verify your email';\n    const text = `Hello ${user.name || ''},\\n\\nClick to verify: ${verificationUrl}\\n\\nThis link expires in 24 hours.`;\n    await sendEmail(user.email, subject, text);\n\n    this.logger.log(`Sent verification to ${user.email}`);\n    return { sent: true };\n  }\n\n  async verify(token: string) {\n    const row = await this.tokenRepo.findOne({ where: { token } });\n    if (!row) throw new Error('Invalid token');\n    if (row.used) throw new Error('Token already used');\n    if (new Date() > row.expires_at) throw new Error('Token expired');\n\n    // Mark token used\n    row.used = true;\n    await this.tokenRepo.save(row);\n    // Set user's email_verified = true handled by controller using user_id from row\n    return row.user_id;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```typescript name=services/auth/auth.controller.ts\nimport { Controller, Post, Body, Get, Query } from '@nestjs/common';\nimport { EmailVerificationService } from './email-verification.service';\nimport { UsersService } from '../users/users.service'; // implement createUser/findUser\n\n@Controller('api/auth')\nexport class AuthController {\n  constructor(\n    private readonly ev: EmailVerificationService,\n    private readonly users: UsersService,\n  ) {}\n\n  @Post('register')\n  async register(@Body() body: any) {\n    // Minimal: create user with email_verified=false\n    const user = await this.users.create({\n      email: body.email,\n      name: body.name,\n      password: body.password, // hash in users service\n      email_verified: false,\n      tenant_id: body.tenant_id\n    });\n    await this.ev.createAndSend(user);\n    return { message: 'User created. Check email to verify.' };\n  }\n\n  @Get('verify-email')\n  async verifyEmail(@Query('token') token: string) {\n    const userId = await this.ev.verify(token);\n    await this.users.markEmailVerified(userId);\n    return { message: 'Email verified. You can now login.' };\n  }\n}\n```\n\n```typescript name=utils/mailer.ts\n// Minimal mailer wrapper. Replace with SendGrid/Mailgun in production.\nimport nodemailer from 'nodemailer';\n\nexport async function sendEmail(to: string, subject: string, text: string) {\n  const transporter = nodemailer.createTransport({\n    host: process.env.SMTP_HOST,\n    port: parseInt(process.env.SMTP_PORT || '587'),\n    secure: false,\n    auth: {\n      user: process.env.SMTP_USER,\n      pass: process.env.SMTP_PASS,\n    },\n  });\n\n  await transporter.sendMail({\n    from: process.env.FROM_EMAIL,\n    to,\n    subject,\n    text,\n  });\n}\n```\n\n```tsx name=apps/admin-portal/pages/admin/settings.tsx\nimport React, { useEffect, useState } from 'react';\nimport axios from 'axios';\n\nexport default function AdminSettings({ initialTenantId }) {\n  const tenantId = initialTenantId || 'REPLACE_TENANT_ID';\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);\n  const [settings, setSettings] = useState(null);\n  const [featureFlags, setFeatureFlags] = useState({});\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    async function load() {\n      setLoading(true);\n      const res = await axios.get(`/api/admin/${tenantId}/settings`);\n      setSettings(res.data.settings || {});\n      setFeatureFlags(res.data.feature_flags || {});\n      setLoading(false);\n    }\n    load();\n  }, [tenantId]);\n\n  if (loading) return <div>Loading...</div>;\n\n  async function save() {\n    await axios.put(`/api/admin/${tenantId}/settings`, { settings, feature_flags: featureFlags });\n    alert('Saved');\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"p-6\">\n      <h1 className=\"text-2xl font-bold mb-4\">Main Admin - Tenant Settings</h1>\n\n      <section className=\"mb-6\">\n        <h2 className=\"font-semibold\">Feature Flags</h2>\n        {['pppoe','hotspot','payments','olts','reseller','white_label','notifications'].map(f => (\n          <div key={f} className=\"flex items-center my-2\">\n            <label className=\"flex-1\">{f}</label>\n            <input\n              type=\"checkbox\"\n              checked={!!featureFlags[f]}\n              onChange={(e) => setFeatureFlags({...featureFlags, [f]: e.target.checked})}\n              />\n          </div>\n        ))}\n      </section>\n\n      <section className=\"mb-6\">\n        <h2 className=\"font-semibold\">Billing</h2>\n        <label>Billing cycle</label>\n        <select value={settings.billing_cycle || 'monthly'} onChange={e => setSettings({...settings, billing_cycle: e.target.value})}>\n          <option value=\"monthly\">Monthly</option>\n          <option value=\"weekly\">Weekly</option>\n          <option value=\"daily\">Daily</option>\n        </select>\n      </section>\n\n      <section className=\"mb-6\">\n        <h2 className=\"font-semibold\">Theme</h2>\n        <label>Primary color</label>\n        <input value={settings.theme?.primaryColor || ''} onChange={e => setSettings({...settings, theme: {...settings.theme, primaryColor: e.target.value}})} />\n      </section>\n\n      <button className=\"px-4 py-2 bg-blue-600 text-white rounded\" onClick={save}>Save Settings</button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nDesign notes / how to wire into existing modules\n- All modules should read tenant settings through a shared SDK or configuration service at runtime (cache in Redis). Example: when Billing Service invoices, check tenant_settings.feature_flags.payments to choose which payment providers are active for that tenant.\n- When provisioning PPPoE, use settings.pppoe.* for speed profiles and quotas.\n- When Hotspot captive portal needs to allow mobile-money login, check feature flag hotspot.mobile_money = true and payments.providers.\n- For OLTs, implement vendor adapters under services/olt/adapters (HuaweiAdapter, ZTEAdapter) that translate common provision calls into device-specific protocols (SSH, NETCONF, RESTCONF). The OltService.provisionOnu method calls the adapter.\n- For multi-country flows, use tenant_countries table; at billing time pick currency per customer or tenant default.\n\nSecurity and sensitive data\n- Store OLT/device credentials in a secrets manager (HashiCorp Vault, AWS Secrets Manager) or encrypt credentials column; do not store plaintext in DB.\n- Protect admin endpoints with strong RBAC; only main admin roles allowed to update tenant_settings.\n- Validate and sanitize all JSON settings before saving.\n\nEmail verification flow summary\n- Register endpoint creates a user with email_verified=false.\n- EmailVerificationService creates a random token stored in email_verification_tokens with expiry.\n- Send verification email with token link.\n- Verify endpoint marks token used and calls users.markEmailVerified(userId).\n- Only allow login if email_verified = true (or allow but mark restricted access until verification).\n\nTesting and rollout plan\n1. Run DB migrations in staging and ensure tenant_settings default handling works.\n2. Deploy SettingsController and Test Admin UI page to staging with an admin user.\n3. Create one tenant and toggle features; confirm other services respond to feature flags (you may add logging to check).\n4. Implement OLT vendor adapter prototype for one vendor and test provisioning on lab device.\n5. Integrate email provider and test verification flows.\n6. Roll out gradually to production; add audit logging for all settings changes.\n\nNext steps I can do for you\n- Option A: If you create the GitHub repo and share the URL, I will push a complete starter commit with the modules above wired into a monorepo scaffold (NestJS + Next.js + TypeORM migrations).\n- Option B: I can generate a full zip of the starter repo here for download (I will paste the rest of files in batches).\n- Option C: I can provide a patch/PR diff you can apply to your existing repository (if you share it).\n\nWhich do you prefer? If you want me to proceed now, tell me:\n- Repo URL (or pick Option B),\n- Preferred backend (NestJS confirmed?),\n- SMTP provider details (for local test you can use Ethereal),\n- Any vendor OLT you want to prototype first (Huawei/ZTE/etc.).",
