      "content": "Direct answer: I rewrote the core pieces you asked for (DB migration + TypeORM Entities + NestJS services/controllers + mailer + a Next.js admin page) and removed the obvious bugs and unsafe patterns from the prior draft. The code below is ready-to-drop-into a NestJS + TypeORM monorepo and a Next.js app with minimal wiring. I included validation, clear error handling, and notes where you must provide environment secrets or small supporting modules (AuthGuard, RolesGuard, UsersService) that are outside the scope of this snippet.\n\nApply these files, run the migration, wire to your NestJS AppModule (register entities and modules), and start. If you want I can produce the full monorepo scaffold next or push to your repo when created.\n\nFiles (copy into your project)\n\n1) DB migration (Postgres)\n```sql name=migrations/20260520_init.sql\n-- Initialize core tables for tenants, tenant_countries, tenant_settings, olts, users, email verification\n-- Run with your migration tool. Make sure pgcrypto extension is available for gen_random_uuid() or replace with uuid_generate_v4()\n\nCREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS \"pgcrypto\";\n\n-- Users (minimal)\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users (\n  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  email text NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  name text,\n  password_hash text NOT NULL,\n  tenant_id uuid,\n  roles text[] DEFAULT ARRAY['CUSTOMER']::text[],\n  email_verified boolean DEFAULT false,\n  created_at timestamptz DEFAULT now(),\n  updated_at timestamptz DEFAULT now()\n);\n\n-- Tenants\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tenants (\n  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  name text NOT NULL,\n  slug text UNIQUE NOT NULL,\n  owner_user_id uuid,\n  created_at timestamptz DEFAULT now(),\n  updated_at timestamptz DEFAULT now()\n);\n\n-- Tenant countries (multi-country mapping)\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tenant_countries (\n  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  tenant_id uuid REFERENCES tenants(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  country_code varchar(3) NOT NULL,\n  currency_code varchar(3) NOT NULL,\n  tax_rate numeric DEFAULT 0,\n  default_country boolean DEFAULT false,\n  created_at timestamptz DEFAULT now(),\n  UNIQUE (tenant_id, country_code)\n);\n\n-- Tenant settings (JSONB for flexibility)\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tenant_settings (\n  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  tenant_id uuid REFERENCES tenants(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  settings jsonb NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}'::jsonb,\n  feature_flags jsonb NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}'::jsonb,\n  created_at timestamptz DEFAULT now(),\n  updated_at timestamptz DEFAULT now(),\n  updated_by uuid\n);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_tenant_settings_tenant ON tenant_settings(tenant_id);\n\n-- OLTs\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS olts (\n  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  tenant_id uuid REFERENCES tenants(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  vendor varchar(64) NOT NULL,\n  name text,\n  host text NOT NULL,\n  port integer,\n  api_type varchar(32) DEFAULT 'ssh',\n  credentials jsonb,\n  region varchar(64),\n  management_url text,\n  enabled boolean DEFAULT true,\n  created_at timestamptz DEFAULT now(),\n  updated_at timestamptz DEFAULT now()\n);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_olts_tenant ON olts(tenant_id);\n\n-- Email verification tokens\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS email_verification_tokens (\n  id uuid PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),\n  user_id uuid REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  token varchar(128) NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  expires_at timestamptz NOT NULL,\n  used boolean DEFAULT false,\n  created_at timestamptz DEFAULT now()\n);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_email_verification_user ON email_verification_tokens(user_id);\n```\n\n2) Entities (TypeORM) — put these under src/entities/\n```ts name=src/entities/user.entity.ts\nimport { Entity, PrimaryGeneratedColumn, Column, CreateDateColumn, UpdateDateColumn } from 'typeorm';\n\n@Entity({ name: 'users' })\nexport class User {\n  @PrimaryGeneratedColumn('uuid')\n  id: string;\n\n  @Column({ unique: true })\n  email: string;\n\n  @Column({ nullable: true })\n  name?: string;\n\n  @Column({ name: 'password_hash' })\n  passwordHash: string;\n\n  @Column({ type: 'uuid', nullable: true })\n  tenantId?: string;\n\n  @Column('text', { array: true, default: () => \"ARRAY['CUSTOMER']::text[]\" })\n  roles: string[];\n\n  @Column({ default: false })\n  emailVerified: boolean;\n\n  @CreateDateColumn({ name: 'created_at' })\n  createdAt: Date;\n\n  @UpdateDateColumn({ name: 'updated_at' })\n  updatedAt: Date;\n}\n```\n\n```ts name=src/entities/tenant.entity.ts\nimport { Entity, PrimaryGeneratedColumn, Column, CreateDateColumn, UpdateDateColumn } from 'typeorm';\n\n@Entity({ name: 'tenants' })\nexport class Tenant {\n  @PrimaryGeneratedColumn('uuid')\n  id: string;\n\n  @Column()\n  name: string;\n\n  @Column({ unique: true })\n  slug: string;\n\n  @Column({ type: 'uuid', nullable: true })\n  ownerUserId?: string;\n\n  @CreateDateColumn({ name: 'created_at' })\n  createdAt: Date;\n\n  @UpdateDateColumn({ name: 'updated_at' })\n  updatedAt: Date;\n}\n```\n\n```ts name=src/entities/tenant-country.entity.ts\nimport { Entity, PrimaryGeneratedColumn, Column, CreateDateColumn } from 'typeorm';\n\n@Entity({ name: 'tenant_countries' })\nexport class TenantCountry {\n  @PrimaryGeneratedColumn('uuid')\n  id: string;\n\n  @Column({ type: 'uuid' })\n  tenantId: string;\n\n  @Column({ length: 3 })\n  countryCode: string;\n\n  @Column({ length: 3 })\n  currencyCode: string;\n\n  @Column({ type: 'numeric', default: 0 })\n  taxRate: number;\n\n  @Column({ default: false })\n  defaultCountry: boolean;\n\n  @CreateDateColumn({ name: 'created_at' })\n  createdAt: Date;\n}\n```\n\n```ts name=src/entities/tenant-settings.entity.ts\nimport { Entity, PrimaryGeneratedColumn, Column, CreateDateColumn, UpdateDateColumn } from 'typeorm';\n\n@Entity({ name: 'tenant_settings' })\nexport class TenantSettings {\n  @PrimaryGeneratedColumn('uuid')\n  id: string;\n\n  @Column({ type: 'uuid' })\n  tenantId: string;\n\n  @Column({ type: 'jsonb', default: '{}' })\n  settings: any;\n\n  @Column({ type: 'jsonb', default: '{}' })\n  featureFlags: any;\n\n  @Column({ type: 'uuid', nullable: true })\n  updatedBy?: string;\n\n  @CreateDateColumn({ name: 'created_at' })\n  createdAt: Date;\n\n  @UpdateDateColumn({ name: 'updated_at' })\n  updatedAt: Date;\n}\n```\n\n```ts name=src/entities/olt.entity.ts\nimport { Entity, PrimaryGeneratedColumn, Column, CreateDateColumn, UpdateDateColumn } from 'typeorm';\n\n@Entity({ name: 'olts' })\nexport class Olt {\n  @PrimaryGeneratedColumn('uuid')\n  id: string;\n\n  @Column({ type: 'uuid' })\n  tenantId: string;\n\n  @Column()\n  vendor: string;\n\n  @Column({ nullable: true })\n  name?: string;\n\n  @Column()\n  host: string;\n\n  @Column({ nullable: true })\n  port?: number;\n\n  @Column({ default: 'ssh' })\n  apiType: string;\n\n  @Column({ type: 'jsonb', nullable: true })\n  credentials?: any;\n\n  @Column({ nullable: true })\n  region?: string;\n\n  @Column({ nullable: true })\n  managementUrl?: string;\n\n  @Column({ default: true })\n  enabled: boolean;\n\n  @CreateDateColumn({ name: 'created_at' })\n  createdAt: Date;\n\n  @UpdateDateColumn({ name: 'updated_at' })\n  updatedAt: Date;\n}\n```\n\n```ts name=src/entities/email-verification-token.entity.ts\nimport { Entity, PrimaryGeneratedColumn, Column, CreateDateColumn } from 'typeorm';\n\n@Entity({ name: 'email_verification_tokens' })\nexport class EmailVerificationToken {\n  @PrimaryGeneratedColumn('uuid')\n  id: string;\n\n  @Column({ type: 'uuid' })\n  userId: string;\n\n  @Column({ unique: true })\n  token: string;\n\n  @Column({ type: 'timestamptz' })\n  expiresAt: Date;\n\n  @Column({ default: false })\n  used: boolean;\n\n  @CreateDateColumn({ name: 'created_at' })\n  createdAt: Date;\n}\n```\n\n3) Settings Service (NestJS) — src/settings/settings.service.ts\n```ts name=src/settings/settings.service.ts\nimport { Injectable, NotFoundException } from '@nestjs/common';\nimport { InjectRepository } from '@nestjs/typeorm';\nimport { Repository } from 'typeorm';\nimport { TenantSettings } from '../entities/tenant-settings.entity';\n\n@Injectable()\nexport class SettingsService {\n  constructor(\n    @InjectRepository(TenantSettings)\n    private readonly repo: Repository<TenantSettings>,\n  ) {}\n\n  async getSettingsForTenant(tenantId: string) {\n    const row = await this.repo.findOne({ where: { tenantId } });\n    if (!row) {\n      return {\n        tenantId,\n        settings: {\n          billing_cycle: 'monthly',\n          currency: 'USD',\n          theme: { primaryColor: '#0ea5e9', darkMode: false },\n          pppoe: { enabled: true },\n          hotspot: { enabled: true },\n          payments: { enabled: true, providers: [] },\n          olts: { enabled: false }\n        },\n        featureFlags: {}\n      };\n    }\n    return row;\n  }\n\n  async upsertSettings(tenantId: string, payload: { settings?: any; featureFlags?: any; updatedBy?: string; }) {\n    let row = await this.repo.findOne({ where: { tenantId } });\n    if (!row) {\n      row = this.repo.create({\n        tenantId,\n        settings: payload.settings || {},\n        featureFlags: payload.featureFlags || {},\n        updatedBy: payload.updatedBy\n      });\n      return this.repo.save(row);\n    }\n    row.settings = { ...row.settings, ...(payload.settings || {}) };\n    row.featureFlags = { ...row.featureFlags, ...(payload.featureFlags || {}) };\n    row.updatedBy = payload.updatedBy;\n    return this.repo.save(row);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n4) DTOs + Controller for Settings — src/settings/settings.controller.ts\n```ts name=src/settings/settings.controller.ts\nimport { Controller, Get, Put, Param, Body, UseGuards, Req, HttpException, HttpStatus } from '@nestjs/common';\nimport { SettingsService } from './settings.service';\nimport { IsObject, IsOptional } from 'class-validator';\nimport { plainToInstance } from 'class-transformer';\n\n// Note: Provide real guards in your app (AuthGuard, RolesGuard).\n// Roles decorator and guards are assumed to exist in your project.\n\nclass UpdateSettingsDto {\n  @IsOptional()\n  @IsObject()\n  settings?: Record<string, any>;\n\n  @IsOptional()\n  @IsObject()\n  featureFlags?: Record<string, any>;\n}\n\n@Controller('api/admin/:tenantId/settings')\nexport class SettingsController {\n  constructor(private readonly settingsService: SettingsService) {}\n\n  @Get()\n  async get(@Param('tenantId') tenantId: string) {\n    if (!tenantId) throw new HttpException('tenantId required', HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);\n    return this.settingsService.getSettingsForTenant(tenantId);\n  }\n\n  @Put()\n  async put(@Param('tenantId') tenantId: string, @Body() body: any, @Req() req: any) {\n    // Validate body\n    const dto = plainToInstance(UpdateSettingsDto, body || {});\n    // class-validator can be used via ValidationPipe at controller level in your app\n    const updated = await this.settingsService.upsertSettings(tenantId, {\n      settings: dto.settings,\n      featureFlags: dto.featureFlags,\n      updatedBy: req.user?.id\n    });\n    return updated;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n5) Email verification service — src/auth/email-verification.service.ts\n```ts name=src/auth/email-verification.service.ts\nimport { Injectable, Logger, HttpException, HttpStatus } from '@nestjs/common';\nimport { InjectRepository } from '@nestjs/typeorm';\nimport { Repository } from 'typeorm';\nimport { EmailVerificationToken } from '../entities/email-verification-token.entity';\nimport { randomBytes } from 'crypto';\nimport * as dayjs from 'dayjs';\nimport { sendEmail } from '../utils/mailer';\n\n@Injectable()\nexport class EmailVerificationService {\n  private readonly logger = new Logger(EmailVerificationService.name);\n\n  constructor(\n    @InjectRepository(EmailVerificationToken)\n    private readonly repo: Repository<EmailVerificationToken>,\n  ) {}\n\n  async createAndSend(user: { id: string; email: string; name?: string }) {\n    const token = randomBytes(24).toString('hex'); // 48 hex chars\n    const expiresAt = dayjs().add(24, 'hour').toDate();\n\n    const row = this.repo.create({\n      userId: user.id,\n      token,\n      expiresAt\n    });\n    await this.repo.save(row);\n\n    const verificationUrl = `${process.env.APP_URL}/auth/verify-email?token=${token}`;\n    const subject = 'Verify your email';\n    const text = `Hi ${user.name || ''},\\n\\nPlease verify your email by clicking the link below:\\n\\n${verificationUrl}\\n\\nThis link expires in 24 hours.\\n\\nIf you did not request this, ignore this email.`;\n\n    await sendEmail(user.email, subject, text).catch(err => {\n      this.logger.error('Failed to send verification email', err);\n      // don't throw — still keep the token so user can request resend\n    });\n\n    this.logger.log(`Verification email created for ${user.email}`);\n    return { sent: true };\n  }\n\n  async verify(token: string) {\n    const row = await this.repo.findOne({ where: { token } });\n    if (!row) throw new HttpException('Invalid token', HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);\n    if (row.used) throw new HttpException('Token already used', HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);\n    if (new Date() > row.expiresAt) throw new HttpException('Token expired', HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);\n\n    row.used = true;\n    await this.repo.save(row);\n    return row.userId;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n6) Minimal UsersService (for register/verify) — src/users/users.service.ts\n```ts name=src/users/users.service.ts\nimport { Injectable } from '@nestjs/common';\nimport { InjectRepository } from '@nestjs/typeorm';\nimport { Repository } from 'typeorm';\nimport { User } from '../entities/user.entity';\nimport * as bcrypt from 'bcrypt';\n\n@Injectable()\nexport class UsersService {\n  constructor(\n    @InjectRepository(User)\n    private readonly repo: Repository<User>,\n  ) {}\n\n  async create(payload: { email: string; name?: string; password: string; tenantId?: string }) {\n    const existing = await this.repo.findOne({ where: { email: payload.email } });\n    if (existing) throw new Error('Email already in use');\n    const passwordHash = await bcrypt.hash(payload.password, 12);\n    const user = this.repo.create({\n      email: payload.email,\n      name: payload.name,\n      passwordHash,\n      tenantId: payload.tenantId,\n      roles: ['CUSTOMER'],\n      emailVerified: false\n    });\n    return this.repo.save(user);\n  }\n\n  async markEmailVerified(userId: string) {\n    const user = await this.repo.findOne({ where: { id: userId } });\n    if (!user) throw new Error('User not found');\n    user.emailVerified = true;\n    return this.repo.save(user);\n  }\n\n  async findByEmail(email: string) {\n    return this.repo.findOne({ where: { email } });\n  }\n}\n```\n\n7) Auth controller (register + verify) — src/auth/auth.controller.ts\n```ts name=src/auth/auth.controller.ts\nimport { Controller, Post, Body, Get, Query, HttpException, HttpStatus } from '@nestjs/common';\nimport { UsersService } from '../users/users.service';\nimport { EmailVerificationService } from './email-verification.service';\n\n@Controller('api/auth')\nexport class AuthController {\n  constructor(\n    private readonly users: UsersService,\n    private readonly ev: EmailVerificationService,\n  ) {}\n\n  @Post('register')\n  async register(@Body() body: { email: string; password: string; name?: string; tenantId?: string; }) {\n    if (!body.email || !body.password) {\n      throw new HttpException('email and password required', HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);\n    }\n    const user = await this.users.create({ email: body.email, password: body.password, name: body.name, tenantId: body.tenantId });\n    await this.ev.createAndSend(user);\n    return { message: 'User created. Verification email sent.' };\n  }\n\n  @Get('verify-email')\n  async verifyEmail(@Query('token') token: string) {\n    if (!token) throw new HttpException('token required', HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);\n    const userId = await this.ev.verify(token);\n    await this.users.markEmailVerified(userId);\n    return { message: 'Email verified' };\n  }\n}\n```\n\n8) Mailer util (nodemailer transport reused) — src/utils/mailer.ts\n```ts name=src/utils/mailer.ts\nimport nodemailer from 'nodemailer';\nimport SMTPTransport from 'nodemailer/lib/smtp-transport';\n\nconst transporter = nodemailer.createTransport({\n  host: process.env.SMTP_HOST,\n  port: Number(process.env.SMTP_PORT || 587),\n  secure: process.env.SMTP_SECURE === 'true', // true for 465, false for other ports\n  auth: process.env.SMTP_USER ? { user: process.env.SMTP_USER, pass: process.env.SMTP_PASS } : undefined,\n  tls: { rejectUnauthorized: process.env.SMTP_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED !== 'false' }\n} as SMTPTransport.Options);\n\nexport async function sendEmail(to: string, subject: string, text: string, html?: string) {\n  if (!process.env.SMTP_HOST) {\n    // In dev you may want to log or use Ethereal\n    console.warn('SMTP not configured, skipping sendEmail. To test, set SMTP_* env vars or use Ethereal.');\n    return;\n  }\n  await transporter.sendMail({\n    from: process.env.FROM_EMAIL || 'no-reply@yourapp.local',\n    to,\n    subject,\n    text,\n    html\n  });\n}\n```\n\n9) Minimal Next.js Admin Settings page — apps/admin-portal/pages/admin/settings.tsx\n```tsx name=apps/admin-portal/pages/admin/settings.tsx\nimport React, { useEffect, useState } from 'react';\n\ntype SettingsPayload = {\n  settings: Record<string, any>;\n  featureFlags: Record<string, boolean>;\n};\n\nexport default function AdminSettings({ tenantId }: { tenantId: string }) {\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);\n  const [payload, setPayload] = useState<SettingsPayload>({ settings: {}, featureFlags: {} });\n  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    if (!tenantId) return;\n    fetch(`/api/admin/${tenantId}/settings`, { credentials: 'include' })\n      .then(async res => {\n        if (!res.ok) throw new Error(await res.text());\n        return res.json();\n      })\n      .then(data => {\n        setPayload({\n          settings: data.settings || {},\n          featureFlags: data.featureFlags || data.feature_flags || {}\n        });\n      })\n      .catch(err => setError(err.message || 'Failed to load'))\n      .finally(() => setLoading(false));\n  }, [tenantId]);\n\n  if (loading) return <div>Loading...</div>;\n  if (error) return <div className=\"text-red-600\">Error: {error}</div>;\n\n  function toggleFeature(flag: string) {\n    setPayload(prev => ({ ...prev, featureFlags: { ...prev.featureFlags, [flag]: !prev.featureFlags[flag] } }));\n  }\n\n  async function save() {\n    try {\n      const res = await fetch(`/api/admin/${tenantId}/settings`, {\n        method: 'PUT',\n        credentials: 'include',\n        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n        body: JSON.stringify({ settings: payload.settings, featureFlags: payload.featureFlags })\n      });\n      if (!res.ok) throw new Error(await res.text());\n      alert('Saved');\n    } catch (err: any) {\n      alert('Save failed: ' + (err.message || err));\n    }\n  }\n\n  const flags = ['pppoe', 'hotspot', 'payments', 'olts', 'reseller', 'white_label', 'notifications'];\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"p-6\">\n      <h1 className=\"text-2xl font-bold mb-4\">Main Admin - Tenant Settings</h1>\n\n      <section className=\"mb-6\">\n        <h2 className=\"font-semibold\">Feature Flags</h2>\n        {flags.map(f => (\n          <div key={f} className=\"flex items-center my-2\">\n            <label className=\"flex-1\">{f}</label>\n            <input\n              type=\"checkbox\"\n              checked={!!payload.featureFlags[f]}\n              onChange={() => toggleFeature(f)}\n            />\n          </div>\n        ))}\n      </section>\n\n      <section className=\"mb-6\">\n        <h2 className=\"font-semibold\">Billing</h2>\n        <label>Billing cycle</label>\n        <select\n          value={payload.settings.billing_cycle || 'monthly'}\n          onChange={e => setPayload(prev => ({ ...prev, settings: { ...prev.settings, billing_cycle: e.target.value } }))}\n        >\n          <option value=\"monthly\">Monthly</option>\n          <option value=\"weekly\">Weekly</option>\n          <option value=\"daily\">Daily</option>\n        </select>\n      </section>\n\n      <section className=\"mb-6\">\n        <h2 className=\"font-semibold\">Theme</h2>\n        <label>Primary color</label>\n        <input\n          value={payload.settings.theme?.primaryColor || ''}\n          onChange={e => setPayload(prev => ({ ...prev, settings: { ...prev.settings, theme: { ...prev.settings.theme, primaryColor: e.target.value } } }))}\n        />\n      </section>\n\n      <button onClick={save} className=\"px-4 py-2 bg-blue-600 text-white rounded\">Save Settings</button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nNotes, safety and wiring\n- Register the new Entities in TypeORM configuration (AppModule) so repositories are available.\n- In production, store device credentials and OLT secrets in a secure vault (HashiCorp Vault, AWS Secrets Manager) rather than raw JSON in DB. If you must store in DB, ensure encryption at application layer.\n- Implement proper AuthGuard and RolesGuard in NestJS and add validation pipe (ValidationPipe) globally so DTOs are validated.\n- CORS + cookie/session: if Next.js talks to NestJS API in another origin, set CORS and Credentials properly.\n- The UsersService here uses bcrypt. Make sure to handle password resets and login flows securely (rate-limits, lockouts).\n- The mailer expects SMTP env vars: SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_USER, SMTP_PASS, FROM_EMAIL, APP_URL.\n- The SettingsController shown omits guards for brevity — you must add UseGuards(AuthGuard, RolesGuard) and a @Roles('SUPER_ADMIN') decorator in your real app.\n- For feature flag propagation, use a runtime config cache (Redis) or shared config service so all microservices pick up changes quickly. SettingsService already supports upsert and you can add a Redis publication on updates.\n\nHow to test quickly\n1. Run the migration SQL on your Postgres DB.\n2. Start NestJS with TypeORM connecting to DB (entities registered).\n3. Create a tenant row and admin user in users table or via API seeded data.\n4. Call POST /api/auth/register to create a user and check email (or log).\n5. Use the Admin settings endpoints to GET/PUT settings and verify responses.\n6. Load the Next.js page (ensure it can call the NestJS API).\n\nIf you want, next I will:\n- Add full RBAC guards and Roles decorator (code).\n- Add a SettingsCacheService that publishes updates to Redis so other services pick them up.\n- Provide vendor OLT adapter examples (Huawei/ZTE) with a small adapter interface and a mock adapter for local testing.\n- Create a GitHub-ready monorepo scaffold and commit all files into it.\n\nWhich next step would you like me to do?",
