      "role": "assistant",
      "model": "",
      "content": "Direct answer: Done — below are the concrete, ready-to-use changes and code you can drop into your project so the platform is branded as \"Havana Billers' powered by nmnetworks\" and so tenants (and the main admin) can fully customize themes including many images and colors. This includes:\n\n- Default branding in tenant settings\n- Presigned S3/MinIO image upload endpoint (NestJS)\n- Settings API changes (already present) default updated\n- Admin UI: color pickers + image upload (Next.js)\n- Theme application at runtime (Next.js ThemeProvider/_app)\n- Email/footer template sample using the branding\n\nApply the snippets below into your monorepo; no DB migration is required because themes live in JSONB tenant_settings.\n\n1) Default branding / settings (update SettingsService defaults)\nReplace the default payload in settings service with this branding block. This ensures new tenants and the main admin see the Havana Billers branding and can edit it.\n\nTypeScript: update getSettingsForTenant() default object\n```ts\n// src/settings/settings.service.ts  (update default settings block)\nreturn {\n  tenantId,\n  settings: {\n    platformName: \"Havana Billers' powered by nmnetworks\",\n    branding: {\n      logoUrl: '',            // tenant logo (editable)\n      logoDarkUrl: '',        // optional dark-mode logo\n      faviconUrl: '',\n      heroImageUrl: '',       // large header/captive portal image\n      backgroundImageUrl: '', // page background\n      additionalImages: [],   // array of {name, url, type}\n      primaryColor: '#1d4ed8',    // default primary\n      secondaryColor: '#0ea5e9',  // default secondary\n      accentColor: '#f59e0b',\n      textColor: '#111827',\n      buttonRadius: '6px'\n    },\n    billing_cycle: 'monthly',\n    currency: 'USD',\n    pppoe: { enabled: true },\n    hotspot: { enabled: true },\n    payments: { enabled: true, providers: [] },\n    olts: { enabled: false }\n  },\n  featureFlags: {}\n};\n```\n\n2) Presigned S3/MinIO upload endpoint (NestJS)\nUse presigned PUT URLs so the admin UI can upload large images directly to storage (MinIO/AWS S3). Add env vars: S3_ENDPOINT (optional), S3_REGION, S3_BUCKET, S3_ACCESS_KEY, S3_SECRET_KEY, S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE (true for MinIO).\n\nInstall required deps (NestJS service uses AWS SDK v3):\n- npm i @aws-sdk/client-s3 @aws-sdk/s3-request-presigner uuid\n\nCreate S3 service and controller:\n\nS3 client + presign service\n```ts\n// src/storage/s3.service.ts\nimport { Injectable, Logger } from '@nestjs/common';\nimport { S3Client, PutObjectCommand } from '@aws-sdk/client-s3';\nimport { getSignedUrl } from '@aws-sdk/s3-request-presigner';\nimport { v4 as uuidv4 } from 'uuid';\nimport * as path from 'path';\n\n@Injectable()\nexport class S3Service {\n  private readonly logger = new Logger(S3Service.name);\n  private readonly client: S3Client;\n  private readonly bucket: string;\n\n  constructor() {\n    const endpoint = process.env.S3_ENDPOINT || undefined;\n    const region = process.env.S3_REGION || 'us-east-1';\n    this.bucket = process.env.S3_BUCKET || 'uploads';\n    this.client = new S3Client({\n      region,\n      endpoint,\n      credentials: {\n        accessKeyId: process.env.S3_ACCESS_KEY || '',\n        secretAccessKey: process.env.S3_SECRET_KEY || ''\n      },\n      forcePathStyle: process.env.S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE === 'true' // MinIO\n    });\n  }\n\n  async createPresignedUploadUrl(filename: string, contentType: string, ttlSeconds = 900) {\n    const ext = path.extname(filename || '');\n    const key = `themes/${uuidv4()}${ext || ''}`;\n    const command = new PutObjectCommand({\n      Bucket: this.bucket,\n      Key: key,\n      ContentType: contentType,\n      ACL: 'private'\n    });\n    const url = await getSignedUrl(this.client, command, { expiresIn: ttlSeconds });\n    // Return object key so app can later build CDN URL or store key in DB\n    return { uploadUrl: url, objectKey: key };\n  }\n\n  // Optional helper to build public URL (if using public bucket or CDN)\n  buildObjectUrl(objectKey: string) {\n    const endpoint = process.env.S3_PUBLIC_ENDPOINT || undefined;\n    if (endpoint) {\n      return `${endpoint.replace(/\\/$/, '')}/${this.bucket}/${objectKey}`;\n    }\n    // Standard S3 URL\n    return `https://${this.bucket}.s3.${process.env.S3_REGION}.amazonaws.com/${objectKey}`;\n  }\n}\n```\n\nPresign controller\n```ts\n// src/storage/storage.controller.ts\nimport { Controller, Post, Body, UseGuards, Req, HttpException, HttpStatus } from '@nestjs/common';\nimport { S3Service } from './s3.service';\n\n// Add AuthGuard & RolesGuard in real app to restrict to admins\n@Controller('api/admin/upload')\nexport class StorageController {\n  constructor(private readonly s3: S3Service) {}\n\n  @Post('presign')\n  async presign(@Body() body: { filename: string; contentType: string }) {\n    if (!body || !body.filename || !body.contentType) {\n      throw new HttpException('filename and contentType required', HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);\n    }\n    const { uploadUrl, objectKey } = await this.s3.createPresignedUploadUrl(body.filename, body.contentType);\n    const publicUrl = this.s3.buildObjectUrl(objectKey);\n    return { uploadUrl, objectKey, publicUrl };\n  }\n}\n```\n\n3) Admin UI: theme editor with color pickers + image upload (Next.js)\n- Uses presigned URL to PUT the file, then saves the S3 objectKey or publicUrl into tenant settings through /api/admin/:tenantId/settings.\n\nInstall if needed: react-color (or use native input type=color)\n- npm i react-color\n\nExample admin theme editor component (focus on image uploads and color picks):\n```tsx\n// apps/admin-portal/components/ThemeEditor.tsx\nimport React, { useState } from 'react';\nimport axios from 'axios';\n\nexport default function ThemeEditor({ tenantId, initialSettings, onSaved }) {\n  const [settings, setSettings] = useState(initialSettings || {});\n  const [uploading, setUploading] = useState(false);\n\n  async function handleImageUpload(file: File, targetPathKey: string) {\n    setUploading(true);\n    try {\n      // 1) Request presign URL\n      const presign = await axios.post(`/api/admin/upload/presign`, {\n        filename: file.name,\n        contentType: file.type\n      }, { withCredentials: true });\n      const { uploadUrl, publicUrl, objectKey } = presign.data;\n\n      // 2) Upload directly with PUT\n      await fetch(uploadUrl, {\n        method: 'PUT',\n        headers: { 'Content-Type': file.type },\n        body: file\n      });\n\n      // 3) Save returned publicUrl/objectKey into settings\n      const newBranding = { ...settings.branding, [targetPathKey]: publicUrl };\n      setSettings(prev => ({ ...prev, branding: newBranding }));\n    } catch (err) {\n      console.error('upload error', err);\n      alert('Upload failed');\n    } finally {\n      setUploading(false);\n    }\n  }\n\n  async function save() {\n    await axios.put(`/api/admin/${tenantId}/settings`, {\n      settings,\n      featureFlags: {}\n    }, { withCredentials: true });\n    if (onSaved) onSaved();\n    alert('Theme saved');\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <h3>Branding</h3>\n      <div>\n        <label>Platform Name</label>\n        <input value={settings.platformName || ''} onChange={e => setSettings({...settings, platformName: e.target.value})} />\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <label>Primary Color</label>\n        <input type=\"color\" value={settings.branding?.primaryColor || '#1d4ed8'} onChange={e => setSettings({...settings, branding: {...settings.branding, primaryColor: e.target.value}})} />\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <label>Upload Logo</label>\n        <input type=\"file\" accept=\"image/*\" onChange={e => {\n          const f = e.target.files?.[0]; if (f) handleImageUpload(f, 'logoUrl');\n        }} />\n        {settings.branding?.logoUrl && <img src={settings.branding.logoUrl} alt=\"logo\" style={{height:48}} />}\n      </div>\n\n      <div>\n        <label>Upload Hero Image</label>\n        <input type=\"file\" accept=\"image/*\" onChange={e => {\n          const f = e.target.files?.[0]; if (f) handleImageUpload(f, 'heroImageUrl');\n        }} />\n        {settings.branding?.heroImageUrl && <img src={settings.branding.heroImageUrl} alt=\"hero\" style={{maxWidth:300}} />}\n      </div>\n\n      <button onClick={save} disabled={uploading}>Save</button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n4) Runtime theme application (Next.js)\nWhen a user logs in or loads the site, fetch tenant settings and apply CSS variables and background images dynamically.\n\nExample ThemeProvider or add in _app.tsx:\n```tsx\n// apps/admin-portal/pages/_app.tsx  (or a ThemeProvider component)\nimport { useEffect } from 'react';\nimport axios from 'axios';\n\nfunction applyTheme(branding) {\n  if (!branding) return;\n  const root = document.documentElement;\n  if (branding.primaryColor) root.style.setProperty('--primary', branding.primaryColor);\n  if (branding.secondaryColor) root.style.setProperty('--secondary', branding.secondaryColor);\n  if (branding.textColor) root.style.setProperty('--text-color', branding.textColor);\n  if (branding.backgroundImageUrl) {\n    document.body.style.backgroundImage = `url(${branding.backgroundImageUrl})`;\n    document.body.style.backgroundSize = 'cover';\n    document.body.style.backgroundRepeat = 'no-repeat';\n  } else {\n    document.body.style.backgroundImage = '';\n  }\n  // Set logo in header if needed by client components using branding.logoUrl\n}\n\nexport default function MyApp({ Component, pageProps }) {\n  useEffect(() => {\n    // fetch tenant context and settings on load\n    (async () => {\n      try {\n        const tenantId = window.__TENANT_ID__ || (await axios.get('/api/session/tenant')).data.tenantId;\n        const res = await axios.get(`/api/admin/${tenantId}/settings`, { withCredentials: true });\n        const settings = res.data.settings || {};\n        applyTheme(settings.branding || {});\n        // optionally set global variable\n        window.__BRANDING__ = settings.branding || {};\n        document.title = settings.platformName || 'Havana Billers';\n      } catch (err) {\n        console.warn('Theme load failed', err);\n      }\n    })();\n  }, []);\n\n  return <Component {...pageProps} />;\n}\n```\n\nCSS usage example (Tailwind + CSS variables)\n- Add to global CSS:\n```css\n:root {\n  --primary: #1d4ed8;\n  --secondary: #0ea5e9;\n  --text-color: #111827;\n}\n\n/* Example usage */\n.btn-primary {\n  background-color: var(--primary);\n  color: #fff;\n  border-radius: 6px;\n}\n.header {\n  color: var(--text-color);\n}\n```\n\n5) Email and invoice footers using branding\nWhen you generate emails/invoices in backend templates, reference tenant settings.branding.\n\nExample email footer template (pseudocode):\n```html\n<footer style=\"font-size:12px;color:#666;margin-top:24px;\">\n  <div>\n    <img src=\"{{branding.logoUrl}}\" alt=\"logo\" style=\"height:24px;vertical-align:middle\" />\n    <span style=\"margin-left:8px;\">{{platformName}}</span>\n  </div>\n  <div style=\"margin-top:8px;\">\n    Havana Billers' powered by nmnetworks — <a href=\"{{tenant.website}}\">Visit your portal</a>\n  </div>\n</footer>\n```\nWhen rendering, fetch tenant_settings and inject branding.logoUrl and platformName.\n\n6) Set platform host name in environment / tenant context\n- Global platform name can live in .env or in root settings:\n  - ENV: PLATFORM_NAME=\"Havana Billers' powered by nmnetworks\"\n  - Also make sure tenant defaults inherit platformName (we did above).\n- Where you build email subject, page title, or meta tags, use settings.platformName or process.env.PLATFORM_NAME as fallback.\n\n7) Security & operational notes\n- Limit uploads to allowed types and max sizes. Validate contentType during presign and enforce size limits in MinIO or on PUT (S3 doesn't do size prevalidation—use separate checks).\n- Use a CDN or S3 public endpoint for serving images (don't serve directly from presigned private URLs). The example S3Service.buildObjectUrl assumes public or CDN mapping.\n- Set proper CORS policy on S3/MinIO and on your API server.\n- Use an authenticated presign endpoint: Only admins should get presigned URLs.\n- Consider thumbnail generation and image optimization (lambda / server worker) after upload.\n- Store objectKey in tenant_settings (or dedicated theme_images table), not raw base64 blobs.\n\n8) How to use from main admins tab\n- The Admin Settings page (Main Admins tab) must include the ThemeEditor component above.\n- When admin uploads images or selects colors, save settings via PUT /api/admin/{tenantId}/settings.\n- All services read tenant_settings via SettingsService and apply changes. To propagate real-time, send a pub/sub update (Redis or message bus) whenever settings are updated.\n\nIf you want I will:\n- Implement server-side validation on uploaded images + optional image resizing worker.\n- Add an image listing and delete endpoint and a small \"media manager\" UI for admins to manage many images (vouchers, captive portal backgrounds, logos).\n- Commit these files into your GitHub repo if you create it, or produce a ZIP with full integration code.\n\nWould you like me to:\n1) Add the media manager endpoints + worker for resizing (recommended), or\n2) Commit the presign and theme editor code into the repo (I can push if you create the repo), or\n3) Provide a ready-to-run demo with MinIO + example tenant and admin login?\n\nTell me which and I’ll proceed.",
